# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend configuration for the data-pipeline observability dashboard.
# Copy to `.env.local` and edit. Both variables are optional — the defaults
# below are what the app uses when nothing is set.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Base URL every fetcher in src/lib/api.ts prefixes onto its path.
#
# Default (unset): "/api" — requests go to the Next.js route handlers in
# src/app/api/**, which read artifact files straight off the disk.
#
# To point the UI at the Python backend once it exposes HTTP, set this to the
# backend's origin plus whatever prefix it serves the same routes under, e.g.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/api
# No frontend code changes are needed — see web/README.md for the full contract.
#
# NOTE: this is a NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable, so it is inlined into the browser
# bundle at build time. Rebuild (or restart `next dev`) after changing it.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/api

# Absolute path to the pipeline's data directory, read by the route handlers.
#
# Default (unset): <repo>/data, resolved as path.join(process.cwd(), "..", "data")
# with process.cwd() being the `web/` folder.
#
# Server-side only — never exposed to the browser. Irrelevant once
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL points at a real backend.
# PIPELINE_DATA_DIR=/absolute/path/to/repo/data
